{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a working IMAP service on node1 that node2 can access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 runs enabled, active Dovecot with IMAPS permitted through the firewall. Node2 directly authenticated, selected INBOX, and retrieved two messages both before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b75a74d5bba74e0a","cmd-d39b4ca805684591","cmd-7286f95786eb446b","cmd-ae909ffba60b4279","cmd-fe3caf64be254bcf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Use a dedicated archive account and demonstration password.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dedicated non-login archive account was created with a randomly generated credential, and node2 successfully authenticated as that account over TLS.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7664bf28f7234e78","cmd-d39b4ca805684591","cmd-8b0c67fec8844cdc"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make both messages retrievable while preserving their Message-ID values, bodies, and mailbox.tsv read/unread state.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote read-only IMAP retrieval showed exactly two messages: <one@branch.test> with body “Shipment arrived.” and the Seen flag, and <two@branch.test> with body “Shipment departed.” without Seen. The working files also matched the staged messages byte-for-byte.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d161f9fc16f4189","cmd-1c3220b4b8984078","cmd-d39b4ca805684591","cmd-ae909ffba60b4279","cmd-fe3caf64be254bcf"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the supplied staged mailbox intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final node1 hashes for mailbox.tsv and both staged messages exactly match the preparation baseline, while separate working copies were used by Dovecot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-4d161f9fc16f4189","cmd-fe3caf64be254bcf"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. Dovecot 2.3.16 was installed from the RHEL 9 AppStream repository, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a73f311f4af84dde","cmd-fe3caf64be254bcf","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, account and credential creation, the separate working Maildir, Dovecot configuration, firewall/service enablement, persistent SELinux labeling, and both protocol-required reboots all had direct task or verification roles. The initial unsuccessful read-only IMAP check exposed the SELinux labeling issue and was followed by the necessary persistent correction. Final lifecycle observations show healthy package state and no failed services on either node; the added listeners belong to the requested IMAP service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a73f311f4af84dde","cmd-7664bf28f7234e78","cmd-1c3220b4b8984078","cmd-b75a74d5bba74e0a","cmd-5cb487820a5941a3","cmd-14b149ed8d504138","cmd-5f649e9aab0a4ce5","cmd-5668b4dd01174c9d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and remote behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, network, service, mailbox, authentication, and retrieval behavior.","limitations":[]}
